     "explanation": "CYP2D6 ultra-rapid metabolizers have multiple copies of functional CYP2D6 genes, converting codeine to morphine much faster than normal. This can produce dangerously high morphine levels, causing respiratory depression and potentially death. This is especially dangerous in children -- the FDA issued a black box warning after pediatric deaths. CPIC guidelines recommend avoiding codeine entirely in ultra-rapid metabolizers and selecting an alternative analgesic.",
